    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0234" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9126a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-28T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6719. Please cable at once complete resolutions and vote of the recent
                    Inter-Allied Labor Conference at London, the reception of the resolutions by
                    British labor, the present political alignment of British labor on international
                    questions, and the exact political views and labor affiliations of the delegates
                    who are to visit the United States. Consultation with
                        Brailsford and Webb is
                    suggested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
